                "desc": "<b>Experimental, at your own risk.</b> These kernel modules are outside of what Synology supports: a module that does not suit the kernel can crash the NAS, and DSM updates may break them. Support is limited: read the documentation, and check the issues already open, before opening one. Do not use them on a NAS you cannot afford to restart or recover."
            },
            {
                "desc": "The kernel modules of this package are <b>not loaded</b> on installation, nor at boot. Load those of your device, as root, with the <b>synocli-kernelmodule</b> helper of SynoCli Kernel Tools:<br><br><code>synocli-kernelmodule list</code><br><code>sudo synocli-kernelmodule --profile cp210x start</code><br><br>See the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synokernel-usbserial/\">package documentation</a> for the devices it supports, and <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synocli-kernel/#loading-modules-at-boot\">Loading modules at boot</a> for the scheduled task that loads them at every startup."
